  "doctrine": [],
  "note": "Arabic qamḥ and Maltese qamħ name the wheat itself. In Hebrew the noun names its milled product and can also describe meal made from barley. Kogan, Proto-Semitic Lexicon §9.6.1, compares the early spelling in the Ebla vocabulary (VE 169), Tigre qəḥəm ‘flour’ and Geʿez qamḥ ‘produce, yield’."
